	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/plain" rect="(20.0, 20.0, 540.0, 82.0)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="13">PRAKTIKUM 3 — EDA

Correlations outputs a FEATURES channel as well as Data. That is how the
Scatter Plot below knows which pair to show. Double-click the link to inspect it.</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/plain" rect="(620.0, 90.0, 330.0, 190.0)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="13">WHAT TO DO
1. Distributions: set variable to 'harga'. Is it skewed?
   Now split by 'kecamatan'.
2. Correlations: which pair is strongest? Click it and
   watch the Scatter Plot follow.
3. Box Plot: 'harga' grouped by 'sertifikat'.
4. SIMPSON HUNT: in Box Plot, put 'harga' by
   'kecamatan', then add a Subgroup. Does any
   comparison reverse once you condition?

Compare everything with notebook week03_eda.ipynb.</text>
